# stackcone Solutions posts

When the user pastes a **problem statement** or asks to create a **solution post**, produce a full Solutions brief in `solutions/` — same visual system as `blog/` (charts, pipelines, tables, SEO).

## Deliverables (always)

1. `solutions/{slug}.html` — published page
2. `solutions/{slug}.md` — markdown source (mirror of content)
3. Update `solutions/solutions.json` — add entry
4. Update `sitemap.xml` — add `<url>` for the new HTML page

**Slug:** lowercase, hyphenated, derived from problem (e.g. `partner-api-oauth`, `rag-internal-copilot`). HTML filename = `{slug}.html`.

## solutions.json entry

```json
{
  "id": "{slug}",
  "title": "Short outcome-focused title",
  "description": "One sentence: problem + approach (under ~155 chars)",
  "href": "./{slug}.html",
  "date": "YYYY-MM-DD",
  "dateLabel": "Month YYYY",
  "category": "RAG | Data | API | Mobile | Docs | Platform",
  "tags": ["3–6 tags"],
  "client": "Company name if mentioned, else omit field"
}
```

## Article page structure (required sections)

Use `blog-page` body, `blog-article` wrapper, `../styles.css` + `../blog/blog.css` + `solutions.css`, `/site-nav.js`, `/script.js`.

| Section | ID | Content |
|---------|-----|---------|
| Title + meta | — | H1 title; `<p class="meta">By Amar Kumar</p>` (no date) |
| Summary | — | 2–3 sentences on the problem and outcome |
| Table of contents | `.toc` | Links to all major sections below |
| Problem | `#problem` | Context, pain points, constraints, who is affected |
| Requirements | `#requirements` | Bulleted functional + non-functional requirements |
| Architecture | `#architecture` | System diagram + data flow; **UML-style ASCII** in `<div class="arch-diagram"><pre>` **and** a `.pipeline` flow for the main path |
| Stack | `#stack` | Table: layer → technology → role |
| Implementation plan | `#implementation` | Phased plan in `.impl-phase` blocks (Phase 1–N with deliverables) |
| What we built | `#what-we-built` | Concrete deliverables list (5+ bullets when company named) |
| Charts | — | **At least 2** Chart.js charts in `.chart-wrap` (e.g. latency breakdown, component map, rollout phases) |
| Glossary | `#glossary` | Key terms table |
| CTA | `.blog-cta` | Same Upwork + Contact pattern as blog posts |

## When a **company name** is mentioned

Go **in depth** — this is a client-style brief:

- Set `client` in `solutions.json`
- Name the company in Problem (as scenario context, not marketing fluff)
- Architecture: full component diagram (API, DB, queues, external systems, auth, observability)
- Implementation: **4–6 phases** with timelines, risks, and rollback notes
- What we built: specific integrations, SLAs, ops runbooks
- Extra chart: e.g. deployment topology or request lifecycle

Do **not** invent confidential internals; describe a **credible production architecture** that fits the stated problem.

## HTML conventions (match blog)

- SEO: unique title, meta description, canonical, OG/Twitter, JSON-LD `Article` + `BreadcrumbList` (Home → Solutions → title)
- Code: `<pre><code>` with span classes `.kw`, `.fn`, `.str`, `.cm` where used in blog
- Pipelines: `.pipeline` > `.pipeline-step` + `.pipeline-arrow`
- Charts: Chart.js CDN at bottom; `chart-wrap` + caption; palette `['#2563eb', '#7c3aed', '#db2777', '#ea580c', '#16a34a', '#0891b2']`
- Links: relative to solutions (`../contact/`, other solution/blog pages)
- Author in JSON-LD can stay organization-focused; visible meta line is **By Amar Kumar**

